RT-08 (MG10 part 3): the card blitter on by default, in bounded bands
(build-tree patch, applied after rt07c-zeroline-bias.patch; built as s13rt04).

MG10 on metal: a blitter operation stalls the 68060 for its whole length
(~20 ms for a full screen) and lost 42-44 % of serial input at 9600 and
38400.  The driver runs a ZZ9KIOC_BLITS batch record by record at base
priority, so interrupts are taken between records; the server now splits
every operation into bands of at most -blitmax pixels (whole rows, a
downward copy's bands bottom-up) and needs no kernel change.

  -blitmin  default 1024 (was 0 = never): MG10 kept the 100x100 gains at
            1024 and 4096 and lost them at 16384
  -blitmax  new, default 8192: ~0.16 ms at the measured ~50,000 px/ms, under
            one character time at 38400 (0.26 ms); 0 = no split

A refusal can now come in the middle of a banded operation (a full queue
flushes); the flush draws everything queued on the CPU and the operation's
remaining rows are drawn on the CPU there, never the whole operation again.
Host test: x11/bench/band-test.sh (6930 cases incl. refusals at each flush).
No startx-rtg flags are needed; -blitmin 0 turns the blitter off.

